        html: '<p>Calling the leak a beta implies a snapshot: this is what the game looked like on a given day. It is nothing of the sort. The files were pulled from an internal store that had accumulated work over years, so a map from one period sits beside an entity definition from another and a texture set from a third. Assembling any of it into something playable means reconciling versions that never coexisted in the first place.</p><p>That is exactly why the modding community has spent two decades on it. Projects to restore the leaked chapters are not ports; they are reconstructions, and every one of them has to make judgement calls about which of several incompatible versions of a thing was the intended one. The material documents a process rather than a product, and reading it requires the same care as reading any other incomplete archive.</p>',
